  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(x):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/df22eea4331c47da3047381ca672fd80ebf75118054316fe88c0e2d96dae0d34.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=0$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,0}(2x\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(x)) & =2\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
